EXT. FROZEN LAKE - ICE FISHING HUT - DAWN

A tiny plywood shack on a plain of white. A thin plume of smoke rises from its tin chimney. The sun pushes up behind a dark treeline, spilling pink across the ice.

Inside, four people crowd shoulder to shoulder around a hole in the floor, lines hanging in the black water. A portable stove glows red.

ASTRID BJORKLUND (60s, wool hat, thermos) tends a line with patient fingers.

KWAME ASANTE (30s, ice-auger slung across his back, laughs easily) rubs his gloves over the stove.

LEILA NOURI (20s, scientist, notebook, clipboard) jots numbers beside the hole.

OLD HARTWELL (70s, one-eyed, cap with earflaps) dozes upright in a folding chair, a pipe unlit in his mouth.

KWAME
Astrid, you've got a bite.

ASTRID
I know.

KWAME
You're not reeling.

ASTRID
I'm waiting.

LEILA
What for?

ASTRID
For him to decide.

The line tugs. Astrid lifts it a single inch. The tension goes slack. She sighs.

LEILA
Eleven centimetres of ice at the edge. Nineteen here. It's thickening, Astrid.

ASTRID
It always thickens. Then it stops.

KWAME
Hartwell, wake up. We have fish.

HARTWELL
(eyes closed)
We have no fish.

KWAME
We have a fish.

HARTWELL
We have an optimist.

Kwame grins. Leila writes it down without being asked, and Astrid's mouth twitches.

Outside, a snowmobile growls. The engine cuts. Boots creak. The door swings open on a rush of white air.

A man ducks in, stamping snow: BENEDICT OYELARAN (40s, ranger's parka, radio on his chest). He closes the door and stands there, enjoying the heat.

KWAME (CONT'D)
Ranger Benedict. Come to arrest us?

BENEDICT
Only if you've got more than the limit.

LEILA
We have none.

BENEDICT
Then you're safe.

ASTRID
Coffee?

BENEDICT
God, yes.

She pours him a cup. He cradles it, steaming, and looks at the four of them: hats, noses, gloves, the black circle of water.

BENEDICT (CONT'D)
Anybody catch anything?

HARTWELL
Not yet.

KWAME
But the day is young, Hartwell.

HARTWELL
The day's old as the lake.

Kwame laughs. Leila turns a page. The stove ticks. Astrid's line twitches again, and nobody says a word.

FADE OUT.
